nexus-release sign: OpenSSL 3 interoperability transcript (TC-SM-16, CON-6, WI 1.4)

A .sig written by `nexus-release sign` verifies with stock OpenSSL 3
`pkeyutl -verify -rawin -pubin` against the key `nexus-release pubkey` prints.
TC-SM-16 repeats this check on every run where OpenSSL 3 is installed and
skips, naming this file, where it is not.

Setup: nexus-release built from cmd/nexus-release (`go build -o $BIN
./cmd/nexus-release`, on PATH); K a scratch directory (mode 0700) outside the
repository, deleted afterwards, holding a throwaway key selected through
$NEXUS_RELEASE_KEY, so the default ~/.config/nexus/release-signing.key is
never read or written; OPENSSL=/opt/homebrew/opt/openssl@3/bin/openssl.
The public key is turned into SPKI PEM by prefixing the fixed 12-byte Ed25519
SubjectPublicKeyInfo header 302a300506032b6570032100 to the raw 32 bytes.
Recorded 2026-11-13 on macOS (darwin/arm64). Output follows verbatim; the
scratch key path is shown as $K.

$ $OPENSSL version
OpenSSL 3.6.1 27 Jan 2026 (Library: OpenSSL 3.6.1 27 Jan 2026)
$ mkdir -p src/fixture && printf "nexus-release sign transcript fixture\n" > src/fixture/hello.txt
$ tar -C src -czf test.tar.gz fixture
$ NEXUS_RELEASE_KEY=$K/release-signing.key nexus-release keygen
nexus-release: wrote $K/release-signing.key (mode 0600). Add this line to providers.nexusd.update in nexusd.yaml on each host:
trustedKeys: ["/hygOxpDlusum4VEYAfmHKUi+lVM2jjGwzq1ZFcCPVE="]
$ ls -l $K/release-signing.key | cut -c1-10
-rw-------
$ NEXUS_RELEASE_KEY=$K/release-signing.key nexus-release check-key
nexus-release: $K/release-signing.key: an ed25519 signing key; public key /hygOxpDlusum4VEYAfmHKUi+lVM2jjGwzq1ZFcCPVE=
$ nexus-release sign --key $K/release-signing.key test.tar.gz
nexus-release: signed test.tar.gz -> test.tar.gz.sig
$ cat test.tar.gz.sig
bD4xkvSbhNObXzQOpHY2GfU3YvSJqRWSQnCaauMFDvzFw1Fo+bse6ADBBRl3AGNnw5NgXkqg+gzUZ8nSU7llCQ==
$ NEXUS_RELEASE_KEY=$K/release-signing.key nexus-release pubkey > pub.b64; cat pub.b64
/hygOxpDlusum4VEYAfmHKUi+lVM2jjGwzq1ZFcCPVE=
$ nexus-release verify --pubkey "$(cat pub.b64)" test.tar.gz
nexus-release: test.tar.gz: signature verified
$ { printf "nexus-release-signature-v1\0"; $OPENSSL dgst -sha256 -binary test.tar.gz; } > msg.bin
$ wc -c < msg.bin
      59
$ tr -d "\n" < test.tar.gz.sig | $OPENSSL base64 -d -A > sig.bin
$ wc -c < sig.bin
      64
$ { printf "\x30\x2a\x30\x05\x06\x03\x2b\x65\x70\x03\x21\x00"; tr -d "\n" < pub.b64 | $OPENSSL base64 -d -A; } | $OPENSSL pkey -pubin -inform DER -out pub.pem
$ cat pub.pem
-----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----
MCowBQYDK2VwAyEA/hygOxpDlusum4VEYAfmHKUi+lVM2jjGwzq1ZFcCPVE=
-----END PUBLIC KEY-----
$ $OPENSSL pkeyutl -verify -rawin -pubin -inkey pub.pem -in msg.bin -sigfile sig.bin
Signature Verified Successfully
# negative control: one flipped message byte
$ cp msg.bin bad.bin && printf "\xff" | dd of=bad.bin bs=1 seek=58 conv=notrunc 2>/dev/null
$ $OPENSSL pkeyutl -verify -rawin -pubin -inkey pub.pem -in bad.bin -sigfile sig.bin || echo "exit $?"
80BF84F701000000:error:030000EA:digital envelope routines:EVP_DigestVerify:provider signature failure:crypto/evp/m_sigver.c:783:ED25519 digest_verify:
Signature Verification Failure
exit 1
